#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:1
msgid "Release 0.13 (2009-11-05)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:3
msgid "This is primarily a bug fix release. It has some new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:5
msgid "Syntactic sugar for writing nested attribute sets. Instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:7
msgid ""
"    {\n"
"      foo = {\n"
"        bar = 123;\n"
"        xyzzy = true;\n"
"      };\n"
"      a = { b = { c = \"d\"; }; };\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:15
msgid "you can write"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:17
msgid ""
"    {\n"
"      foo.bar = 123;\n"
"      foo.xyzzy = true;\n"
"      a.b.c = \"d\";\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:23
msgid "This is useful, for instance, in NixOS configuration files."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:25
msgid ""
"Support for Nix channels generated by Hydra, the Nix-based continuous build "
"system. (Hydra generates NAR archives on the fly, so the size and hash of "
"these archives isn’t known in advance.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:29
msgid ""
"Support `i686-linux` builds directly on `x86_64-linux` Nix installations. "
"This is implemented using the `personality()` syscall, which causes `uname` "
"to return `i686` in child processes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:33
msgid ""
"Various improvements to the `chroot` support. Building in a `chroot` works "
"quite well now."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:36
msgid ""
"Nix no longer blocks if it tries to build a path and another process is "
"already building the same path. Instead it tries to build another buildable "
"path first. This improves parallelism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:40
msgid "Support for large (\\> 4 GiB) files in NAR archives."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:42
msgid "Various (performance) improvements to the remote build mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:44
msgid ""
"New primops: `builtins.addErrorContext` (to add a string to stack traces — "
"useful for debugging), `builtins.isBool`, `builtins.isString`, `builtins."
"isInt`, `builtins.intersectAttrs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:48
msgid "OpenSolaris support (Sander van der Burg)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:50
msgid ""
"Stack traces are no longer displayed unless the `--show-trace` option is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.13.md:53
msgid ""
"The scoping rules for `inherit                 (e) ...` in recursive "
"attribute sets have changed. The expression _e_ can now refer to the "
"attributes defined in the containing set."
msgstr ""
